<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.6.4: Using Scientific Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01349</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.6.4: Using Scientific Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b3852d9f-f996-4492-b8c7-b95b133f1c74</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>How would you write each of the following numbers in scientific notation?</para>
    <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
      <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis>Decimal Form</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Scientific Notation</emphasis></entry></row>
      <row>
          <entry>
            0.00000654
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            0.0000947
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            683,000
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            0.022
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            5,200
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            0.000352
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    
  
  <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
   </para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
        <entry><emphasis>Decimal Form</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Scientific Notation</emphasis></entry></row>
    <row>
        <entry>
          0.00000654
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(6.54\times10^{-6}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          0.0000947
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(9.47\times10^{-5}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          683,000
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(6.83\times10^5\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          0.022
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(2.2\times10^{-2}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          5,200
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(5.2\times10^3\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          0.000352
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(3.52\times10^{-4}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody></tgroup></table>
  
  

</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>How would you write each of the following scientific notation values in decimal form?</para>
    <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
      <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis>Scientific Notation</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Decimal Form</emphasis></entry></row>
      <row>
          <entry>
            \(7.26\times10^{-4}\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \(3.32\times10^{-2}\)
          </entry>
          <entry>  </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \(9.4\times10^6\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \(8.87\times10^{-1}\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \(6.395\times10^4\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \(4.0\times10^{-3}\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    
  
  <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
   </para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
        <entry><emphasis>Scientific Notation</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Decimal Form</emphasis></entry></row>
    <row>
        <entry>
          \(7.26\times10^{-4}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          0.000726
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \(3.32\times10^{-2}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          0.0332
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \(9.4\times10^6\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          9,400,000
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \(8.87\times10^{-1}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          0.887
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \(6.395\times10^4\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          63,950
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \(4.0\times10^{-3}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          0.004
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody></tgroup></table>
  
  

</solution></exercise>
</example><title>Video: Converting between Scientific Notation and Decimal Form</title>
<para>Watch the following video to learn more about rewriting scientific notation in decimal form and decimal form in
  scientific notation.</para>
